From 7fe6849c3cea2c4ef0a5eeb4018d39aaa2ad7745 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 14:54:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): fence updater reclaims before terminating
 workers [daveey]

Problem: six core-update reclaims in 289 fleet requeues also booked a crash
failure (reported 24h to 2026-11-15 12:47Z).

Why 1: failure observers can close/account a worker killed by the updater.
Why 2: reclaim_task signals and settles process custody before its closing
transaction; the concurrent sweep sees a dead worker and no pause decision.
Why 3: the updater's reason only becomes durable in the post-kill reclaimed
receipt. An EOFError loss is not independently evidence of owner restart.
Root (happened): termination precedes durable ownership of neutral closure.
Root (not caught): handoff regressions test completed reclaimed receipts,
not a second connection observing death inside the terminate/close interval.
Recurrence: the earlier core-update requeue/handoff fixes (2602, 3088 and
preserve review handoffs across updater TERM receipts) recognize completed
pauses; they cannot prevent failure_finalized already emitted before reclaim.

Commit an exact-run/claim/PID/start local reclaim command before signalling.
Crash, expiry and runtime reapers respect that decision. If its executor dies
or unwinds, a subsequent observer resumes the same authorized reclaim,
including process custody, outside the observer write transaction. The intent
never silently expires into a charge. It is an authorized pause decision, not
a retrospective signal/EOF classifier. Retain normal Board lease authority;
no replica writes or retroactive accounting repair. Preserve unrelated strikes
on automatic requeues; ordinary operator reclaim retains its reset behavior.

Affected historical cards (not repaired): t_423c32555af40d11,
t_78b5b9d1c01809c8, t_60e1b62eed385db5, t_ced6e6c9cab0f714,
t_78b1ff930ed8af7c, t_f374b9910f0eb237.

Proof:
- Base d2a8c5cbf25f, new two-order regression: 2 failed; crash-first charged
  1 -> 2, requeue-first cleared existing strike 1 -> 0.
- Local and primary-board ordering, identity, custody exception, abandoned
  reclaimer, expiry/runtime competitor and ordinary SIGTERM controls pass.
- Initial seven focused files: 126 passed; subsequent expanded modern-loss
  coverage plus every owner_recovery importing suite: 352 passed, 15 skipped
  (platform/opt-in real Board integration), 23 files, 108.2s.
- Eight targeted mutants killed, including each identity field, observer hold,
  expiry hold, abandoned recovery and prior-strike preservation.
- scripts/check: 20 checks passed before publication.
- Read-only replica census: 17,242 tasks, zero preexisting intent tables;
  historical rows acquire no exemption. New intents are host-local commands.

Rebased onto main ca1802c8a8 (optional explicit-operator reclaim attribution):
kanban_db.reclaim_task still validates the attribution before any signal or claim
change, then passes it to the extracted reclaim, which adds it to the reclaimed payload.

Task: t_b0780784b2b4dad6. Update cadence/pauses unchanged. Post-deploy replica
query and independent exact-head review remain required before card completion.
